    read-line  : [Console.Read] Text

Page 1

Chapter: RocClosureCapturesTextList
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig,
 "inspect: closure captures string list", case 23 in file order:

     { x = ["captured", "list"] f = |_| x result = f(0) match result { [first, ..] => first, _ => "" } }

 and Roc expects "captured".

 THE TEXT TWIN OF THE PORT THAT RAISED H2. Case 19 is the same program with
 Integer elements and is `roc-closure-captures-list`, whose refusal started
 the whole lambda-parameter thread. This one matters for the reason matrix
 case f matters: every H2 case whose true answer is `Integer` can be passed by
 a backend that is defaulting rather than recovering, and only a `Text` tells
 the two apart. If the Integer twin passes and this one does not, whatever
 recovered the type recovered the DEFAULT.

 ADAPTATION: Roc prints an inspected string with quotes; `print-line-uni`
 prints the text. The `.expected` is `captured`.

Section: Functions

  capture-text : Integer -> Text
  capture-text (n) =
   let x = ["captured", "list"]
   in let f = \ignored -> x
   in list-at (f 0) 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (capture-text 0)
  end
